WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.886
Automaticity is the ability to perform practiced components with reduced conscious effort.

2
00:00:04.886 --> 00:00:08.551
It matters because attention and working memory are limited.

3
00:00:08.551 --> 00:00:17.101
When basic elements of a skill become fluent, the expert has more attention available for higher-level judgment, adaptation, and monitoring.

4
00:00:17.101 --> 00:00:26.059
A skilled performer does not have to think through every tiny step with equal effort, which creates room for more complex decisions.

5
00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:30.131
Fluency can be powerful, but it can also be misleading.

6
00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:34.203
When performance feels easy, people may assume it is correct.

7
00:00:34.203 --> 00:00:37.053
Ease is not the same as accuracy.

8
00:00:37.053 --> 00:00:49.675
An expert may move quickly because the situation fits a well-learned pattern, but that same speed can become risky if the environment changes or if an important exception is hidden.

9
00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:52.525
Automaticity should support judgment, not replace it.

10
00:00:52.525 --> 00:00:54.968
Cognitive load still matters for experts.

11
00:00:54.968 --> 00:01:00.262
High-risk work often includes interruptions, fatigue, ambiguity, time pressure, and competing goals.

12
00:01:00.262 --> 00:01:06.777
Even skilled people can miss routine steps when memory is overloaded or the environment is noisy.

13
00:01:06.777 --> 00:01:12.884
That is why experts still use checklists, procedures, safeguards, peer review, and well-designed tools.

14
00:01:12.884 --> 00:01:18.177
These supports do not insult expertise; they protect it from predictable human limits.

15
00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:23.878
The practical lesson is to automate the right things while keeping critical thinking engaged.

16
00:01:23.878 --> 00:01:29.171
Routine components should become efficient enough that they do not consume all attention.

17
00:01:29.171 --> 00:01:38.943
At the same time, the system should create pauses for verification, escalation, and review when the stakes are high or the pattern is uncertain.

18
00:01:38.943 --> 00:01:41.793
Mature expertise combines fluency with disciplined safeguards.
